1. DEFINITIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

"Framework" means the BlueCube Coder Framework, including all files, commands, 
agents, hooks, configurations, and related materials contained in the .claude/ 
directory.

"Licensed Repository" means a code repository in which this Framework has been 
deployed under a valid subscription and for which applicable Repository Fees 
have been paid.

"Authorised Users" means employees and contractors of Licensee who have access 
to the Licensed Repository and a valid Claude Code license.

"Derivative Works" means modifications, adaptations, or extensions of the 
Framework created by Licensee.

"Expertise Files" means the expertise.yaml files and related outputs generated 
from codebase analysis specific to Licensee's code.

"Learning Levels" means the five progressive levels of AI-assisted development 
maturity: (1) Tool Familiarity, (2) Planned Collaboration, (3) Context-Driven 
Execution, (4) Autonomous Delegation, and (5) Trusted Autonomy.

"Subscription Term" means the period during which Licensee maintains an active 
BlueCube Lab subscription.

